+/*
+ * Command mode: the horizontal blanking only sets the DSI link rate. With the
+ * 48-pixel blanking of the first port the link ran at ~362 Mb/s per lane, so
+ * sending a DSC frame took ~15 ms of the 16.7 ms refresh; a late kickoff let
+ * the panel's scan overtake the transfer and decode a half-written 48-row
+ * slice as a band of colour noise at the top (overlay animations). The front
+ * porch below gives the 60 Hz link rate stock uses (829 Mb/s per lane: byte
+ * clock 103.6 MHz), so a frame goes out in ~6.5 ms. Refresh stays 60 Hz.
+ */
+#define AMS678_HFP	557
